{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1ea97589fc09cc3c9a5e2a5a8c20af49bddfd7f15319a0ec5b417763f9138c6a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the extension market is a folder in this repo served raw from main, so a merged pull request makes an extension installable immediately; contributing one is a JSON file plus a PR."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3824115687f4cc94ace7178046d3b164211a05fda3dee54eac83d040d7f65454"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: highlight queries should be compiled against their grammar and asserted in test/languages.test.ts, since bad queries fail silently."},{"claim_ids":["clm_53db1ddb3fbd397fc41e84bc33f89088fe682ca065ceb7d7586c89e18e455c3a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Settings live in two layers: a global config.json rewritten whole and a per-project .druk/settings.json of overrides that wins after merging."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5ecc33fbadd124697e74a982b0fe802ac7e9e0a3ee0dba791d70824c97974b5e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A filetype may have several language servers and all run concurrently; diagnostics are kept per sender and merged, while feature requests go to each ready server in turn with the first real answer winning."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6e2bc898058983798aa8946eb6f71cdcfab870b15b58d1820581a43bad0cf843"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The app is a Solid application rendered to the terminal by OpenTUI, which supplies layout, text buffer, undo/redo, mouse hit-testing and the tree-sitter worker; the repo is the wiring around it."},{"claim_ids":["clm_917a7ec2031df2d25e238e9f3bd9fc3697cbae2f55d77be1dc75a59512c3db1b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: a boundary test fails the suite if ui/ or feature folders import from app/, enforcing one-way dependency direction."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cc6dfd0780483a2792d13ae3b92ad8c3e0d78e4390d6f2d0638042a3de825313"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Extensions are JSON manifests, never code: ins